# Design Intelligence (offline catalog + brand gates)

Local, zero-network design decision engine. Search a curated catalog, then lock a per-project
design system to a `MASTER.md` that later builds read instead of re-guessing style every time.

## When to Use

- Picking a visual direction for a client site, landing page, dashboard, or deck.
- Choosing an exact palette / font pairing and needing CSS import + Tailwind config.
- Auditing an existing page against UX rules (a11y, forms, motion, anti-patterns).
- At the start of any client build, to persist a design source-of-truth (`MASTER.md`).

## Quick commands

```bash
S=~/.hermes/skills/creative/design-intelligence/scripts/ds.py
python3 $S catalogs                                     # what's in the catalog
python3 $S search "b2b industrial supplier" --catalog styles -n 5
python3 $S search "monochrome" --catalog colors -n 5
python3 $S search "arabic bilingual" --catalog typography -n 5
python3 $S system "bilingual B2B industrial equipment supplier, lead-gen" \
        --stack html-tailwind --persist ~/clients/<name>/site
python3 $S stack html-tailwind "hero section" -n 8
python3 $S system "<query>" --json                      # machine-readable
```

Catalogs: `styles` (88) · `colors` (192) · `products` (192) · `typography` (74) ·
`ux` (119) · `app` (32) · `motion` (17) · `charts` (25) · `icons` (105) · `landing` (34).
Stacks: astro, html-tailwind, nextjs, nuxtjs, react, shadcn, svelte, uno, vue.

## Workflow

1. **Query the catalog** with the *client's business*, not a vibe word — `system` matches on
   product/industry row first, then derives palette, type, UX and motion.
2. **Read `MASTER.md`** it prints. Fix anything that fights the brand gates below.
3. `--persist <dir>` writes `MASTER.md` next to the build; commit it. Re-run only when the
   client's business changes, not per page.
4. **Build against `MASTER.md`**, not from memory. If a choice isn't in the file, add it there.
5. **Deploy preview first** (Cloudflare Pages preview URL), prod only after approval.

## Brand gates — override the catalog, never the other way round

| Gate | Rule |
|---|---|
| Faces | No human faces / living beings in client-facing work. Only exceptions: fire-lab, or Aamir's own approved photo on his own profile. Pick styles that read as abstract/product/architectural, and reject style rows that lean on people-photography. |
| Copy | Client-facing text = pure English, AI-free, zero emoji, one-word brand, never Aamir's name. |
| Iconography | No emoji-as-icon. Use the `icons` catalog (Phosphor/Lucide) with real import code. |
| Top section | Readable brand logo + sharp hero. Blurry upscaled images = fake = rejected. |
| Type floors | Body ≥ 16px, never < 12px; check contrast pairs from the `colors` row (`on-primary` vs `primary`). |
| Bilingual (AR) | Arabic needs its own RTL pairing — don't mirror the Latin font. Keep both editions in one site dir (`ar.html` + `tools/build_ar.py` pattern). |

## Pitfalls

- **Don't install the upstream skill** (7 skills, 812 files, +1.5 MB font/icon dumps). This is the
  project-scoped borrow: data + our own search script, nothing else.
- `search` is keyword + field-weighted, not semantic. Bad query in, bad row out — use the client's
  industry words, then refine with `-n`.
- Style rows overlap by design; take 1 primary + 1 secondary max or the page loses identity.
- `--persist` overwrites an existing `MASTER.md`; it never merges. Keep edits in the file, re-run
  into a scratch dir if you're just exploring.
- Motion catalog is GSAP-flavoured; skip the snippet if the page has no GSAP — take the duration
  and easing only.

